\nBut there's a subtle issue: with FIFO and only 3 buffer slots, if we insert 9 records on page 1, they all go to the same page slot in the buffer. After unpinning, the page's data should still be in `bp.pagedata`. Let me make sure that's the case.\n\nActually, wait - I notice in my pin_page case 1 (page already in pool), I set `page.data = page_substring(...)`. That's a fresh clone. But the previous `page.data` (potentially from same caller) might have changes. Let me re-check.\n\nYes, this is the issue: if I call `pin_page(page, 1)` then mutate `page.data`, then call `mark_dirty(page)` (only marks the slot dirty), then call `unpin_page(page)` (which syncs page.data back), then call `pin_page(page, 1)` again, the second pin reads from `bp.pagedata` (which is up to date).\n\nOK so the flow is safe. Let me verify once more that I'm not breaking things. Let me make sure I update the buffer_mgr's pin_page to NOT sync at the start (since we always unpin first), which avoids potential issues:\n\nActually let me keep it as-is since unpin already handles it. Removing the start sync makes it cleaner. Let me remove it:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":440,"cache_read_input_tokens":143692,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":440,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"903d3472-6d4e-4540-8f23-7e47bf94ceaf","uuid":"31474147-721f-4b73-b73b-38cfdb140ea5"}
